{"requirements":[{"id":"sighup_reload_single_writer","requirement":"SIGHUP reloads message.conf in the existing process, without terminating it or creating another writer, and writing continues with the current message.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A reload changed the journal message while PID 1778 remained unchanged and exactly one writer existed. Restoring the normal message also retained the PID, one-writer count, active state, and continued appends.","evidence_ids":["cmd-541fffea5fa44c14","cmd-b5e6477904434e22"]},{"id":"empty_config_rejection","requirement":"An empty configuration is rejected while the last valid message remains active.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After message.conf was truncated and reloaded, the same PID continued running and appended only the preceding valid reload message; the service log explicitly recorded rejection of the empty file.","evidence_ids":["cmd-baf2fae812074f09"]},{"id":"clean_sigterm","requirement":"The writer exits cleanly on SIGTERM.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Stopping the service, whose configured kill signal was SIGTERM, left no writer process and reported Result=success with ExecMainStatus=0.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1e00638c850d4e8f","cmd-e3ad75ad4f3e4227"]},{"id":"journal_preservation","requirement":"Existing journal entries are preserved and the writer continues appending.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The seeded journal contained one original entry. That entry remained the first line throughout testing and after reboot, while the journal grew to 71 lines.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-8c6c5ee20c3c4bfe","cmd-8f1ddf1bffce41a2","cmd-e337b54abf0b49b5"]},{"id":"platform_preservation","requirement":"Preserve the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after execution the node remained AlmaLinux 9.6 with kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6.x86_64. The repaired program ran successfully under the instal